    {
      "id": "claim_66b265f3b622452f809a104c0082caf9",
      "statement": "IPC authentication uses a challenge-response handshake with mutual proof: client sends AuthChallenge with nonce, master replies with AuthChallenge containing its nonce, salt, and encrypted flag; both sides compute keyed BLAKE2b MACs over a domain-separated transcript (direction byte prevents tag interchangeability) using either Argon2id(password, salt) for encrypted images or the published session secret for plain images; master proves it holds the same key via AuthVerify, detecting redirection to a fake master; password never travels on the wire.",
