    {
      "id": "claim_411bc7860e274aabbbad234d53e2ad3f",
      "statement": "Poison-recovered locks (lock_unpoisoned, read_unpoisoned) are used for mutexes guarding reconstructible in-memory state (session registry, IPC client pool, auto-defrag config, async flush pending ranges, decoded blob cache) where a panic mid-critical-section cannot leave data inconsistent; propagating poison would permanently brick the subsystem. DiskManagerInner RwLock deliberately propagates poison because a panic there could leave on-disk structures inconsistent.",
